lus add-ons to 2031 &mdash; a genuinely startling sentence three years ago. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Thomas Kristensen</span><span>&nbsp;was in Bergamo for a medical on 12 August, joining </span><span style="font-weight:700">Atalanta</span><span>&nbsp;from </span><span style="font-weight:700">Udinese</span><span>&nbsp;on a loan with an obligation at &euro;22m plus &euro;3m, Udinese keeping 10 per cent of a future sale. And a chain runs through Tuscany: </span><span style="font-weight:700">Roberto Piccoli</span><span>&nbsp;to </span><span style="font-weight:700">Bologna</span><span>&nbsp;(loan with an &euro;18m obligation, 10 per cent sell-on), which unlocks </span><span style="font-weight:700">Mateo Pellegrino</span><span>&nbsp;from </span><span style="font-weight:700">Parma</span><span>&nbsp;to </span><span style="font-weight:700">Fiorentina</span><span>&nbsp;at around &euro;24m, which in turn frees </span><span style="font-weight:700">Thijs Dallinga</span><span>&nbsp;to go to </span><span style="font-weight:700">1. FC K&ouml;ln</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;on loan with an option.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span>The messiest file in Italy is </span><span style="font-weight:700">Rodrigo Mora</span><span>, the </span><span style="font-weight:700">FC Porto</span><span>&nbsp;forward wanted by </span><span style="font-weight:700">Roma</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">. In seventy-two hours, four incompatible structures were published: a &euro;5m loan plus &euro;45m option; a &euro;7&ndash;8m loan plus a &euro;42&ndash;43m obligation totalling &euro;50m; a co-ownership at &euro;25m for half the registration; and &euro;25m plus 40 per cent of a future sale. Roma have insisted on no buy-back. This paper is not going to print a number. Status: advanced talks; fee genuinely unestablished.</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span>One more, for the connoisseurs. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Juventus</span><span>&nbsp;want a goalkeeper and the mechanism proposed is baroque: </span><span style="font-weight:700">PSG</span><span>&nbsp;buy </span><span style="font-weight:700">Zion Suzuki</span><span>&nbsp;permanently from </span><span style="font-weight:700">Parma</span><span>&nbsp;for around &euro;35m &mdash; </span><span style="font-weight:700">Romano</span><span>&nbsp;gave that strand a &ldquo;here we go&rdquo; on 11 August, with </span><span style="font-weight:700">Foot Mercato</span><span>&nbsp;reporting a five-year deal &mdash; and then loan him straight to Turin for 2026/27. Suzuki is said to be hesitant about signing for one club and playing for another, which is a reasonable position. Juventus are simultaneously in advanced talks for </span><span style="font-weight:700">Jhon Lucum&iacute;</span><span>&nbsp;of </span><span style="font-weight:700">Bologna</span><span>: personal terms agreed on 11 August, Bologna asking &euro;20m plus bonuses, Juventus offering &euro;18m plus </span><span style="font-weight:700">Juan Cabal</span><span>&nbsp;as a makeweight. And </span><span style="font-weight:700">Du&scaron;an Vlahovi&#263;</span><span>, released by Juventus, signed a three-year deal at </span><span style="font-weight:700">Be&scaron;ikta&scaron;</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;on 12 August.</span></p><h3 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">PSG rebuild the front line; Marseille are being taken apart by the accountants</span></h3><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:italic">One French club is spending European champions&rsquo; money. Another is selling everyone it owns because a regulator told it to.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Paris Saint-Germain</span><span>&nbsp;have turned over their attack. Out went </span><span style="font-weight:700">Gon&ccedil;alo Ramos</span><span>&nbsp;to </span><span style="font-weight:700">AC Milan</span><span>&nbsp;for a club-record sale &mdash; PSG confirmed the move; the fee is reported between &euro;70m and &euro;74m &mdash; plus </span><span style="font-weight:700">Randal Kolo Muani</span><span>&nbsp;to </span><span style="font-weight:700">Juventus</span><span>&nbsp;(&euro;38m or &euro;41.2m, unreconciled) and </span><span style="font-weight:700">Kang-in Lee</span><span>&nbsp;to </span><span style="font-weight:700">Atl&eacute;tico Madrid</span><span>&nbsp;at &euro;40m. In came </span><span style="font-weight:700">Maghnes Akliouche</span><span>&nbsp;from </span><span style="font-weight:700">Monaco</span><span>&nbsp;on 6 August for a package reported at &euro;50m including bonuses, a five-year deal to 2031 and the No. 11 shirt &mdash; </span><span style="font-style:italic">&ldquo;Signer au Paris Saint-Germain est une immense fiert&eacute;,&rdquo;</span><span>&nbsp;he said &mdash; plus </span><span style="font-weight:700">Lucas Digne</span><span>&nbsp;from </span><span style="font-weight:700">Aston Villa</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;on 9 August. Ferran Torres and Suzuki, above, would make five and six.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Olympique de Marseille</span><span>&nbsp;are doing the opposite, and not by choice. The DNCG&rsquo;s ruling of 26 June imposed an </span><span style="font-style:italic">&ldquo;encadrement de la masse salariale et des indemnit&eacute;s de mutations&rdquo;</span><span>&nbsp;&mdash; a cap on both wages and transfer spending &mdash; after several seasons of nine-figure outlay. The consequence has been a summer-long liquidation: </span><span style="font-weight:700">Mason Greenwood</span><span>&nbsp;to </span><span style="font-weight:700">Fenerbah&ccedil;e</span><span>&nbsp;for a reported &euro;39&ndash;40m, </span><span style="font-weight:700">Pierre-Emerick Aubameyang</span><span>&nbsp;to </span><span style="font-weight:700">Deportivo</span><span>, and inside this window </span><span style="font-weight:700">Facundo Medina</span><span>&nbsp;to </span><span style="font-weight:700">Bayer Leverkusen</span><span>&nbsp;on 11 August (&euro;23m plus &euro;2m, five years) and </span><span style="font-weight:700">Ger&oacute;nimo Rulli</span><span>&nbsp;to </span><span style="font-weight:700">Manchester City</span><span>&nbsp;on 12 August for &euro;3.5m. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Nayef Aguerd</span><span>&nbsp;passed a medical at </span><span style="font-weight:700">Real Sociedad</span><span>&nbsp;on 12 August &mdash; a loan with an option, a year after OM paid &euro;23m for him. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Olympique Lyonnais</span><span>&nbsp;and </span><span style="font-weight:700">Monaco</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;are also under salary-mass supervision.</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span>The biggest live French story is a teenager. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Ayyoub Bouaddi</span><span>, eighteen, of </span><span style="font-weight:700">Lille</span><span>, is wanted by </span><span style="font-weight:700">Manchester City</span><span>&nbsp;as the long-term answer to the Rodri question. The Spanish daily </span><span style="font-weight:700">AS</span><span>&nbsp;put the price at &euro;130m and described the deal as &ldquo;en excellente voie&rdquo;; Foot Mercato&rsquo;s own line is more cautious &mdash; &ldquo;plus de 100 M&euro;.&rdquo; Treat &euro;130m as a newspaper number, not a club-confirmed one. Status: advanced talks, price unverified. Also live: </span><span style="font-weight:700">Folarin Balogun</span><span>, Monaco to </span><span style="font-weight:700">Tottenham</span><span>, with </span><span style="font-weight:700">L&rsquo;&eacute;quipe</span><span>&nbsp;reporting discussions opened and an estimate around &euro;60m. And </span><span style="font-weight:700">Paul Pogba</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">, 33, is now a free agent: Monaco moved to terminate after a fresh thigh injury in training on 11 August, having got six appearances out of him last season.</span></p><h3 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">MLS shops the veteran aisle: Lozano to the Galaxy, Alexis S&aacute;nchez to Montr&eacute;al</span></h3><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:italic">The secondary window is open until 2 September and the roster rules were loosened for exactly this.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span>The most eye-catching move of the week was intra-league: </span><span style="font-weight:700">Hirving &ldquo;Chucky&rdquo; Lozano</span><span>&nbsp;joined the </span><span style="font-weight:700">LA Galaxy</span><span>&nbsp;on loan from </span><span style="font-weight:700">San Diego FC</span><span>&nbsp;on </span><span style="font-weight:700">7 August</span><span>, through December 2026, as a Designated Player with an option to make it permanent. General manager </span><span style="font-weight:700">Will Kuntz</span><span>: </span><span style="font-style:italic">&ldquo;Hirving is a player whom we tried to acquire three years ago, so this feels like something of a full circle moment.&rdquo;</span><span>&nbsp;The Galaxy also signed </span><span style="font-weight:700">Sergi Roberto</span><span>&nbsp;on a free from </span><span style="font-weight:700">Como</span><span>&nbsp;on 8 August, through June 2028 with an option, and sold </span><span style="font-weight:700">Edwin Cerrillo</span><span>&nbsp;to </span><span style="font-weight:700">Club Am&eacute;rica</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;the same day.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">CF Montr&eacute;al</span><span>&nbsp;signed </span><span style="font-weight:700">Alexis S&aacute;nchez</span><span>&nbsp;as a free agent from </span><span style="font-weight:700">Sevilla</span><span>&nbsp;on 11 August, as a Designated Player through 2027 with an option. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Houston Dynamo</span><span>&nbsp;took </span><span style="font-weight:700">Marcelo Saracchi</span><span>&nbsp;from </span><span style="font-weight:700">Boca Juniors</span><span>&nbsp;through 2028&ndash;29. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Vancouver Whitecaps</span><span>&nbsp;added the 21-year-old Serb </span><span style="font-weight:700">Aleksa Cvetkovi&#263;</span><span>&nbsp;from </span><span style="font-weight:700">OFK Beograd</span><span>&nbsp;on 12 August under the U-22 Initiative. Two DP slots have just opened and both clubs have said so on the record: </span><span style="font-weight:700">Atlanta United</span><span>, after loaning </span><span style="font-weight:700">Emmanuel Latte Lath</span><span>&nbsp;to </span><span style="font-weight:700">Union Berlin</span><span>&nbsp;&mdash; chief soccer officer </span><span style="font-weight:700">Chris Henderson</span><span>: &ldquo;This move also opens up a Designated Player spot for us which we will look to fill in this summer window&rdquo; &mdash; and </span><span style="font-weight:700">St. Louis CITY</span><span>, after selling </span><span style="font-weight:700">Marcel Hartel</span><span>&nbsp;to </span><span style="font-weight:700">Hannover 96</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;on 11 August.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span>Traffic runs the other way too. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Max Arfsten</span><span>&nbsp;left </span><span style="font-weight:700">Columbus Crew</span><span>&nbsp;for </span><span style="font-weight:700">Middlesbrough</span><span>&nbsp;on 4 August with the Crew retaining a sell-on; </span><span style="font-weight:700">Olwethu Makhanya</span><span>, the </span><span style="font-weight:700">Philadelphia Union</span><span>&rsquo;s first-ever U22 Initiative signing, has an agreed move to </span><span style="font-weight:700">Rangers</span><span>. And for context on the scale of what MLS is now buying: </span><span style="font-weight:700">Robert Lewandowski</span><span>&nbsp;joined the </span><span style="font-weight:700">Chicago Fire</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;from Barcelona on 29 June as a Franchise Player through 2027&ndash;28, and scored his first Leagues Cup goal on 9 August.</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12.8pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#0f7a4e;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">THE RUMOUR MILL</span></p><h4 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:12pt;padding-bottom:12.8pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#0f2e22;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">What is simmering, and how hot</span></h4><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:italic">Everything below is unresolved as of 12:00 Pacific on Wednesday. Certainty is stated for each. Nothing here is official.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Cristian Romero, Tottenham &rarr; Atl&eacute;tico Madrid.</span><span>&nbsp;The best-sourced saga in Europe not involving Rodri. Atl&eacute;tico&rsquo;s opening &euro;30m was rejected; Spurs want &euro;40m. Per </span><span style="font-weight:700">Esto es Atleti</span><span>&nbsp;on 11 August, the clubs and the agents have been meeting since Monday and &ldquo;lo que queda por cerrar es el salario y los bonus de la operaci&oacute;n, no la voluntad del jugador.&rdquo; </span><span style="font-weight:700">Romano</span><span>&nbsp;reports Inter&rsquo;s &euro;40m alternative collapsed when they could not sell </span><span style="font-weight:700">Benjamin Pavard</span><span>, and that Romero has given Atl&eacute;tico the green light. </span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Personal terms agreed; clubs apart on fee.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Bradley Barcola, PSG &rarr; Liverpool.</span><span>&nbsp;Framed as the succession to </span><span style="font-weight:700">Mohamed Salah</span><span>, who left Anfield this summer. Quoted around &pound;130m. Romano reported on 10 August that PSG had responded to Liverpool&rsquo;s indicated proposal and that club-to-club talks are live. </span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Concrete interest; no agreem